---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ProjectPageHeader from '../ProjectPageHeader.astro';
import ProjectSection from '../ProjectSection.astro';
import ProjectList from '../ProjectList.astro';
import ProjectProse from '../ProjectProse.astro';
import TagList from '../TagList.astro';
---

<Base title="Krution / Kacper Noniewicz" description="A read-mostly web UI for the Kor stack: Kron jobs, Korpus records and live Kor events in one Go binary.">
  <div class="py-16 pb-20">
    <ProjectPageHeader label="Go / MIT / Release planned" title="Krution" intro="A small, read-mostly web UI for the Kor stack. One Go binary with the front end embedded, showing what Kron is running, what Korpus has stored and what is moving over Kor right now." />

    <div class="max-w-180">
      <ProjectSection title="What it does">
        <ProjectList items={[
          "Kron: loaded jobs with their triggers, next run, last status and run history, plus the schedules stored in Korpus with their upcoming fire times",
          "Korpus: every registered record type with its JSON Schema fields, and a paginated, read-only record browser",
          "Kor: the handler catalog from kor.describe and a live tail of publications over server-sent events, filterable by subject pattern",
          "A step graph for each schedule, built from its stored action",
        ]} />
      </ProjectSection>

      <ProjectSection title="Read-only by default">
        <ProjectProse>
          <p>Krution stores nothing and schedules nothing; it is a viewer. The only mutations, run-now and enable/disable, exist only when the server starts in write mode. Otherwise the controls are not rendered at all, rather than rendered and disabled. There is deliberately no form for calling arbitrary handlers.</p>
        </ProjectProse>
      </ProjectSection>

      <ProjectSection title="Stack">
        <TagList tags={["Go", "Kor", "Korpus", "Kron", "Server-sent events"]} />
      </ProjectSection>

      <ProjectSection title="Status">
        <ProjectProse>
          <p>Working against my own Kor stack. Planned for release alongside <a href="/projects/kor/">Kor</a>, <a href="/projects/korpus/">Korpus</a> and <a href="/projects/kron/">Kron</a>.</p>
        </ProjectProse>
      </ProjectSection>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
